From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:16:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: support Giantec GT9764BA in the DW9768 actuator
 driver

GT9764BA uses the DW9768 register layout, SMBus word ordering, and
vin/vdd supplies. Add the GT9764BA compatible to the existing driver
and reuse its probe, controls, media entity, runtime PM integration,
and register access.

Keep the Piano bidirectional motor's neutral position, raw AAC
settings and 50-step 10 ms parking. Retain the previous readback,
position recovery, and power-retention behavior after an I2C failure.
DW9768 and GT9769 continue to use their existing profile. Preserve the
gt9764 V4L2 entity name and a gt9764 module alias for existing callers.

The initialization and parking sequence is from the Piano
OS3.0.309.0.WPYCNXM factory actuator module and the published GT9764
driver.

Link: https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/blob/a369d30bd5df3fcfb4304ee9e7ae10fa4f11899a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lens/vcm/v4l2/gt9764/gt9764.c
Link: https://github.com/slwyts/Project-SunUEFI/commit/442088b170459b8fbd838aa6ced3b683e98ba9ca
Link: https://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/torvalds/linux.git/tree/drivers/media/i2c/dw9768.c?id=65e4fd942f72a9dba0e4e257290c4fa1aa756854
Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Co-developed-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
Signed-off-by: Cryolitia PukNgae <cryolitia.pukngae@linux.dev>
